codelaw-rules-security-python

This pack holds no rule yet; every rule it will hold is written for
codelaw.
Rules ported from Bandit (Apache-2.0) and Ruff's `S` rules (MIT) name their source rule in `ported_from:` and
are listed here with that tool's version and licence when they land
(SR-RULE-PACKS decision 7).

Rule sets under a copyleft or source-available licence — eslint-plugin-no-unsanitized
(MPL-2.0), njsscan (LGPL-3.0), Semgrep's rules (the Semgrep Rules License) — are
read for ideas only; no text, pattern or code is taken from them (L2).
